course: dictionary
lesson: 12126
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists them, and the sentence tells you which one to use. «Mia's dog was her comforter when she felt sad.» Here a comforter is something that makes you feel better, because the dog made Mia feel better.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «Grandma tucked a thick comforter over my bed on the cold night.» The words bed and cold tell you this comforter is a warm cover, not a person. Always ask: what does the rest of the sentence tell me?
explain: Some meanings are old-fashioned. «The baby sucked her comforter and fell asleep.» In old British English, a comforter was a baby's dummy, a soother to suck on. Words change over time, so a dictionary tells you when a meaning is old.
explain: Words can also come from a book of faith. «Job's comforters» is a phrase from the Bible for friends who try to help but end up making you feel worse. Use the sentence and the dictionary together to find the right meaning.
fact: A comforter is a person or thing that comforts someone who is sad or worried.
fact: In American English, a comforter is a thick, warm quilt for a bed.
fact: In old British English, a comforter was a long woollen scarf, or a baby's dummy.
fact: In some Bible translations, «the Comforter» is a name for the Holy Spirit, who Christians believe comforts and helps them.
fact: «Job's comforters» means friends who make you feel worse.
exercise: «When Sam was sad, his best friend sat with him and was a real comforter.» What is a comforter in this sentence? | *A person who makes someone who is sad feel better | A hard seat for sitting on | A tool for fixing bikes | A loud bell that rings at noon
exercise: «Dad pulled the thick comforter up over my bed on the snowy night.» What is a comforter here? | A baby's dummy | A long woollen scarf for walking | A cold drink | *A warm quilt for a bed
exercise: Which Bible phrase means friends who make you feel worse? | *Job's comforters | Noah's ark | David's harp | Good Samaritans
test: «The baby sucked her comforter and fell asleep, as babies did long ago.» What is a comforter in this sentence? | A scarf for a cold day | *A baby's dummy, a soother to suck | A soft pillow | A quilt for a bed
test: «Tom's dog was a comforter to him every night when he felt lonely.» What does comforter mean here? | *A thing or person that comforts someone who is sad | A bed cover | A long scarf
exam: In some Bible translations, what is «the Comforter»? | *A name for the Holy Spirit, who Christians believe comforts and helps them | A king who ruled long ago | A bell in a church tower | A name for a shepherd
